<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">African Americans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">African Americans are Americans of wholly or partly sub-Saharan African descent, most of them descendants of people enslaved in what became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> from the seventeenth century until abolition in 1865. In the nineteenth century some free African Americans emigrated to escape discrimination, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> in the 1820s and to Liberia, founded for them by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society">American Colonization Society</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/african-americans.jpg" alt="African Americans" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tweedle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Americans_2020_County.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
